x19181 text "Two different jobs, stated in each row. One edit, warm session: A0 applies the edit in process on a session that is already open, and the others are whole-project checks that start a fresh process every time, wall time. Whole front end, fresh process: both sides start cold and check everything, the like-for-like row, which A0 loses on macOS. On Linux that row is the shipped command, `a0 check` of the release executable; the macOS row predates it and times a node process that imports the checker. The same front end is 4,103 lines in A0 and 637 lines in TypeScript. The macOS and Windows edit times were recorded before edits were validated incrementally (results/edit-incremental.json: 7.24 ms before and 1.82 ms after, median of the same 14 edits). Windows was measured on a saturated machine, so tsc and tsgo moved by several times between runs there: read the Windows rows as contended and do not compare them as ratios."
